{"id":"ithamar","name":"Ithamar","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ithamar"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ithamar","text":"Palm isle, the fourth and youngest son of Aaron (1 Chr. 6:3). He was consecrated to the priesthood along with his brothers (Ex. 6:23); and after the death of Nadab and Abihu, he and Eleazar alone discharged the functions of that office (Lev. 10:6, 12; Num. 3:4). He and his family occupied the position of common priest till the high priesthood passed into his family in the person of Eli (1 Kings 2:27), the reasons for which are not recorded. (See ZADOK.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H385","lemma":"אִיתָמָר","xlit":"ʼÎythâmâr","gloss":"Ithamar, a son of Aaron","kjv":"Ithamar","count":13,"share":0.48},{"strong":"H499","lemma":"אֶלְעָזָר","xlit":"ʼElʻâzâr","gloss":"Elazar, the name of seven Israelites","kjv":"Eleazar","count":10,"share":0.37},{"strong":"H175","lemma":"אַהֲרוֹן","xlit":"ʼAhărôwn","gloss":"Aharon, the brother of Moses","kjv":"Aaron","count":9,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H30","lemma":"אֲבִיהוּא","xlit":"ʼĂbîyhûwʼ","gloss":"Abihu, a son of Aaron","kjv":"Abihu","count":5,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H5070","lemma":"נָדָב","xlit":"Nâdâb","gloss":"Nadab, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Nadab","count":5,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H5656","lemma":"עֲבֹדָה","xlit":"ʻăbôdâh","gloss":"work of any kind","kjv":"act, bondage, bondservant, effect","count":5,"share":0.19}],"verses":["Exod.6.23","Exod.28.1","Exod.38.21","Lev.10.6","Num.4.28","Num.7.8","1Chr.6.3","1Chr.24.1","1Chr.24.2","1Chr.24.3","1Chr.24.4","1Chr.24.5","1Chr.24.6","Lev.10.7","1Chr.24.7","1Chr.24.8","1Chr.24.9","1Chr.24.10","1Chr.24.11","1Chr.24.12","1Chr.24.13","1Chr.24.14","1Chr.24.15","1Chr.24.16","1Chr.24.17","1Chr.24.18","1Chr.24.19"],"related":[{"id":"eleazar-eleazer","type":"cooccur","shared":21,"jaccard":0.438,"why":"21 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"lot","type":"cooccur","shared":15,"jaccard":0.115,"why":"15 verses are indexed under